From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:58:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Summarize Session -- a precise summary to copy, or
 to start a thread or a sub-thread from

Operator, 2026-11-25: a way to compile the session's content and context
into a precise, organized summary, with options to copy it or to open a new
thread or a sub-thread with it as the content. Asked to check Claude Code's
own commands first: none hands a summary out. /compact summarizes, but
replaces the session's own context; /recap is one line; /export needs the
CLI's terminal UI and is not reachable over ACP; /branch and /fork copy the
conversation without summarizing it.

The agent panel's options menu gains "Summarize Session", which opens a card
above the composer, where /btw's card sits, with two sources (the operator
chose both):

- Local, the default (session_digest.rs): the thread's entries put in order
  without asking the agent -- the requests, the last answer, the files
  changed (only edits that completed; a failed edit is listed as failed and
  a refused one not at all), the commands run, what failed, the plan with
  its open steps, what is still running, the files read, and how often the
  context was compacted. No tokens; the same thread gives the same text.
  It is an index, not a synthesis.
- By the agent: the agent writes the summary as a /btw side question
  (_claude/btw, Claude Agent (Plus) 0.38.0), so it reads the session's whole
  context and the answer never enters the conversation. Offered only when
  the agent advertises side questions. The request asks for Goal, What was
  done, Files changed, Current state, Open items, Constraints, in the user's
  language, inventing nothing.

The card's actions take the source on screen: Copy; New Thread, a thread of
the same agent whose composer holds the summary, unsent
(new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt); Sub-thread, story 039's clean sub-thread,
linked under this thread in the sidebar, the summary quoted in its composer.

New Thread and Sub-thread open after the click, deferred (window.defer): the
click is still updating this ThreadView, and opening a thread makes the
panel keep the one leaving the screen -- this one, when it is running --
which reads it. Seen on Xvfb as a double-lease panic before the deferral.
A sub-thread's link shows in the sidebar after its first message, as story
039's clean sub-thread always has.

Logs: session_summary_opened (items, chars), session_summary_agent
(outcome, chars), session_summary_open (sub_thread, chars) -- lengths only,
never the text.

Tests: session_digest_tests.rs (the digest's rules) and
thread_view/tests/session_summary_tests.rs (the card reads the thread as it
is; an agent without side questions offers only the local summary; Copy
takes the text on screen; New Thread and Sub-thread close the card). The
panic above was not reproducible in the test harness -- its stub agent never
reaches the panel's keep-the-running-thread path -- so the Xvfb proof is
its evidence. The agent source has no stub answering side
questions, so it is covered by the live test.

In the claude-agent-acp-plus group, at its end.
---

